<title>TURKEY: Turkish Yapi Kredi mandates UBS for $150 mln loan.</title>
<headline>Turkish Yapi Kredi mandates UBS for $150 mln loan.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's Yapi ve Kredi Bankasi mandated the Union Bank of Switzerland (UBS) to arrange a one-year $150-million syndicated loan, bank officials said on Friday.</p>
<p>They said the pre-export financing facility, Yapi Kredi's first foreign loan deal for the past three years, was fully underwritten by UBS.</p>
<p>Officials did not elaborate.</p>
</text>
